A("Z2047","interesting","Ran the step (C code, primes ≤ 2·10⁵) for the four sign patterns t·u·v ± u ± v with 4 | t. Pattern −− is exactly the (★) family: its failures are the 7 (★)-zeros (409, 577, 5569, 9601, 23929, 83449, 102001). Pattern ++ fails only at 5, 13, 17, 97, 113, 193, 449 among p ≡ 1 (4), and no prime p ≡ 1 (4) above 449 is missed. Mixed-sign patterns fail only at p=5. So the sign flip, not the 4|t constraint, separates a thin infinite failure set from a finite one.",["scripts/z52b_p1_U09_cont.c","data/z52b/pass1/U09/cont_out.txt","BRAINSTORM/z52b_pass1_U09.md"],"Extend the ++ pattern to p ≤ 10⁷ and identify which u ≥ 2 witnesses are needed beyond u = 1 (u = 1 needs p−1 to have a divisor ≡ 1 mod 4 in [5,(p−1)/2]); then test whether ++ has finitely many exceptions.")
